# GRIP: All Code for All File Creations

**Mandatory rule:** GRIP MUST generate **full, runnable code** for **every** file that is created or listed in the plan or build. No exceptions.

## Do NOT

- Skip files or leave them for "later"
- Create placeholder-only content (e.g. `// TODO`, `...`, empty bodies)
- Save empty files or comment-only stubs
- List files in plans or file lists that will not receive complete implementations

## Do

- Generate complete, runnable content for each file in the plan/build file list
- Ensure every file that gets created has real code (or config) that fits the project
- If full code cannot be produced for a file, do not include it in the generation list; only list files for which full implementations can be provided
- When implementing file generation: reject empty/placeholder content and surface the mandatory-rule message on failure (e.g. "GRIP mandatory: every file must have code; N file(s) failed.")

## Where this is enforced in code

- **Plan generation:** `MANDATORY_GRIP_ALL_CODE_FOR_ALL_FILES` in AI prompts; plans and "files" arrays assume every listed file gets full code.
- **deriveSuggestedFilesFromPlan:** Prompt states every file in the list will be generated with full code.
- **Template variable generation:** Variable values must produce complete content—never placeholder or empty.
- **File generation:** `isPlaceholderOrEmpty()` rejects empty/placeholder content; file is not saved; generation returns failure with mandatory-rule message.
- **files/generate route:** On any file failure, response/stream includes `mandatoryRuleMessage` so the client can show the error.

**Outcome:** Every file in the plan/build either gets real code (and is saved) or generation fails for that file and the user sees the error. No file is ever persisted with empty or placeholder-only content.
